  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Updated the Excel.Report.PDF dependency to 0.36.0. Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.8.1.\n(0.8.3) Mail: the SendGrid sender (SendGridSettings / SendGridMailSender, v3 mail/send REST) is now public, verified by real sending. Bulk sending uses native personalizations (up to 1000 recipients per request) with server-side {variable} substitutions, so SendGrid is the recommended infrastructure for large campaigns. The sender address must be verified in SendGrid (Single Sender Verification or domain authentication). Wire it in your app's MailSenderTable with a \"SendGrid\" configuration section.\n(0.8.2) Mail preview HTML: a variable that resolved to an empty value was rendered as a large box overlapping the toolbar (CSS class collision with the \"no recipients\" placeholder). It is now shown as a small \"(empty)\" mark inline.\n(0.8.1) Compatibility: the 0.5.0 mail API (SmtpMailService / MailSettings, together with ScriptObjects.MailService / MailMessage in Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.8.0) is available again, so projects created from the 0.5.0 templates build and run unchanged after upgrading. SmtpMailService now sends through SmtpMailSender (MailKit). Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras 0.8.0.\nNote for custom code that passes an untyped [] or null as the storage list to TemporaryFileManager / StorageAccess (since 0.8.0): the IEnumerable<IFileStorage> overloads make that call ambiguous - pass Array.Empty<IFileStorage>() (typed FileStorage[] variables, as in the templates, are unaffected).",
